7. Market Microstructure Safeguards: Adverse Selection Mitigation
To prevent grid inventory accumulation during heavy directional breakouts or crashes, the AI implements a Dynamic Re-Centering Module:
 * Momentum Detection: Real-time monitoring of order book imbalance and short-timeframe Exponential Moving Averages (EMAs).
 * Grid Dragging: If directional momentum exceeds a pre-programmed standard deviation threshold, the AI instantly cancels all open limit orders, halting the grid.
 * Re-anchoring: The system waits for volatility to settle, establishes a new baseline price, and deploys a fresh grid around the new center to prevent toxic inventory drag.
